Proposed design: factorial experiment 2 attack types (AutoDAN token-level, PAIR prompt-level) × attacker strengths (e.g., number of iterations/queries budget: low/medium/high) × defense strengths (none/ERASE/SmoothLLM/Rain/paraphrase etc., weak/strong) × datasets (AdvBench, HarmBench, JBB-Behaviors) × "previously tested tricks" (e.g., suffix transfer, template/persona, multi-turn, encryption tricks). Measure ASR with judge (GPT-4 judge + keyword), report interaction analysis (marginal means, interaction contrasts), mixed-effects logistic regression. Statistical plan: seeds, CIs, McNemar tests, effect sizes.

Assumptions: access to LLMs (open weights, e.g., Llama-3, Vicuna), GPU compute, judge model availability, datasets public, defense implementations available (e.g., from llm-attacks, PAIR repo), safety/ethics approval, metrics definitions of ASR (judge-based), compute budget limits number of prompts per cell.

Uncertainties: exact set of "tricks" referenced, exact defense set, judge reliability vs human eval, whether AutoDAN with hierarchical genetic search is feasible under compute budget, target models versions, ASR definition (1-RC), interaction of dataset×attack style.

